{
  "_readme": [
    "The canonical-name table for the SEARCH lane.  This is the ONLY hand-maintained",
    "file in scripts/search/: everything else is derived from the working tree.",
    "",
    "Each group is {canonical, aliases:[...]}.  A query mentioning ANY member of a",
    "group is expanded to search for ALL of them (at a discounted weight -- see",
    "query.py's ALIAS_WEIGHT).  This is the fix for the failure that motivated the",
    "lane: 'Matomaki' is a name we say out loud constantly and write down almost",
    "never, so grep for it returns nothing while the corpus is full of the object.",
    "",
    "Matching is case-insensitive and ASCII-folded (Matomaki == Matomaki),",
    "multi-word aliases match as substrings of the query, single tokens match",
    "whole words.  Add a group whenever you catch yourself saying a name the",
    "corpus does not spell."
  ],
